New: Make the variable-coefficient INS integrators read bdry_interp_type ("LINEAR" or "QUADRATIC") and pass their boundary treatment to the objects they create or serve: the Stokes operator and preconditioner, both halves of the viscous term, the velocity and pressure subdomain solvers, the divergence-free velocity extension, and the velocity boundary conditions, including the TRACTION value of IBAMR::INSVCStaggeredVelocityBcCoef beyond a corner with a velocity boundary. Overrides, errors, and the plog report of differing treatments are as in IBAMR::INSStaggeredHierarchyIntegrator. IBAMR::VCStaggeredStokesProjectionPreconditioner and IBTK::VCSCViscousOperator use the extrapolation type of the boundary treatment. The plog report includes the mass and momentum integrator of the conservative form.
<br>
